 "The Cell Door": "",
 ", x, 100); g.fillText(": "",
 "Prison guard": "",
 "Aagh! My eyes! A star in his hand!": "",
 "The sun! At night! I can’t see!": "",
 "Crito has a plan. Socrates has an argument.": "",
 "Crito is waiting in the Agora of Athens. Something has happened to Socrates.": "",
 "Crito has bad news": "",
 "You’re going to rescue Socrates from his own principles. This I have to see.": "",
 "Night has fallen. Go to the prison south of the Agora": "",
 "Wait with Crito for nightfall": "",
 "You’ve been seen! Fight the guards!": "",
 "Get to Socrates’ cell without being seen. Stay out of the guards’ sight; a flashlight (F) in the face dazzles them": "",
 "Stealth: the yellow cones are where the guards are looking.": "",
 "Intruder! At the cells! Get him!": "",
 "The Cell Door: open the jailer’s lock": "",
 "Work the lock": "",
 "The Laws: convince Socrates to come with you": "",
 "Crito. And our friend with the glass eyes. You’re up early. Or late.": "",
 "Let us examine it first. Should we listen to the opinion of the many, or to the one who knows?": "",
 "“Your friends will be shamed. People will say we let you die to save money.”": "",
 "Why should we care so much what the many think? The reasonable ones will understand what really happened.": "",
 "“Your sons need their father.”": "",
 "And what will they learn from a father who runs from the laws that raised him? My friends will care for them, if they are friends.": "",
 "“The verdict was unjust. You don’t owe it anything.”": "",
 "“And now, because the verdict displeases you, you will destroy us, as far as one man can?” What would I answer them, friend?": "",
 "Grab his arm. “I’ll carry you out if I have to.”": "",
 "“…I don’t have an answer for the Laws.”": "",
 "Get out before the whole watch arrives!": "",
 "The cell is open! Stop them!": "",
 "The Crito": "",
 "You tried. Socrates stayed, by his own choice.": "",
 "In Kosmopolis the sacred ship cannot find its way home: the sentence waits.": "",
 "Next: the Lyceum. Bring the dog.": "",
 "Day one. Or year one, I can’t tell. I woke in a square of marble with a burn on my hand and Grandpa’s book in my bag. The car is in pieces, everywhere. I will fix it alone. How hard can it be?": "",
 "The roads fold. I walked for a week and arrived where I began. A boy with a map asked me what I was looking for. I told him to mind his own business. I regret that.": "",
 "The air here goes thick and thin. I built a lung from bronze and old leather to steady it. It worked. I stamped it with Grandpa’s workshop name, out of habit, or homesickness.": "",
 "I asked Thales nothing. I was too busy. I asked Pythagoras nothing either. I tuned their machine to the car’s cycle and walked away while they were still arguing.": "",
 "Eleven years. I fixed their bridge and they carved “the Stranger” on it. Nobody here knows my name. I am starting to forget it myself.": "",
 "I sold a priest a mirror trick today. I needed the money. I told him a young one would come and set it right. I don’t know yet if that is a prophecy or a plan.": "",
 "I understand now. I can’t fix it. I never could, not alone. But a younger me could, if the road were laid out for him, one philosopher at a time, the way Grandpa wanted to teach me and I never let him.": "",
 "I switched the Coupling to Strife with my own hands. I left a note. It is the cruellest thing I have ever done, and the most necessary. He will hate me. Good. Hate is a kind of attention.": "",
 "The boy is coming. I’ve put the key with the only person in Athens who will make him work for it.": "",
 "I left Grandpa’s book in Abdera. I’ve read it so many times the pages are soft. Diogenes is in the foreword. I wonder if the boy has noticed that the old dog follows him everywhere.": "",
 "Xanthippe looked at me like she could see the whole plan. Maybe she could. She’s the only one who asked me a question I couldn’t answer: “And who is mending your roof?”": "",
 "I put my own face in the shadows. Old, tired, sad. If he sees it in time, maybe he never becomes it.": "",
 "He laughed in the car. I remember that laugh. Good.": "",
 "Pick up a page of a journal": "",
 "You could read the rest now. He’s written ahead, I can see the ink. Or you could burn it and find out like a man.": "",
 "Read ahead.": "",
