 "The priests call it a sacred idol of Poseidon. They’ve built it a little altar.": "",
 "Take it back.": "",
 "The shepherd rings it and his goat comes running. “A charm that calls goats home.”": "",
 "Tangled in a fisherman’s net. He thinks it’s the tail of a sea serpent.": "",
 "Trade him a fish-hook for it (the phone never runs flat again).": "",
 "A sculptor wears them to stare at the sun. “Eyes of night,” he calls them.": "",
 "Stuck all over a column of the stoa. People read them as messages from the gods. One says, in Nico’s own writing: “fix capacitor, call Grandpa?”": "",
 "The Pythagoreans keep it as a perfect circle. It isn’t, quite.": "",
 "In Aristotle’s specimen jar, labelled “unknown seashell”. It’s from 2026. And it’s older than you are here.": "",
 "The watchers called its beam “the fire of the gods”. The batteries still work, just.": "",
 "Grandpa Leo’s reading glasses, the ones with the cracked left lens. Nico puts them in his pocket and says nothing for a long while.": "",
 "Polaroid photo": "",
 "Under Diogenes’ straw: a faded photo of a boy and an old man laughing in a workshop. Nico and Grandpa Leo. Diogenes calls it “a tiny painting”.": "",
