 "Ten pieces of your world, scattered through mine. Your people carry a great deal of rubbish. I like them better already.": "",
 "Echoes of Tomorrow": "",
 " of 10 objects from the workshop found.": "",
 "Two brothers": "",
 "We still argue. But we argue at the same table now.": "",
 "One farm, two of us. I worked the land for ten years. He paid off our father’s debts with his own money. Who deserves the farm, stranger?": "",
 "The one who worked the land: the farm is the work.": "",
 "The one who paid: without him there’d be no farm to work.": "",
 "Both: share it, and the harvest.": "",
 "Still my ship. Or still Theseus’ ship. I sleep fine either way, now.": "",
 "This is the ship of Theseus. Over the years I’ve replaced every plank. Every one. The city wants it as a monument. Is it still the same ship?": "",
 "No. Not one piece of it is the original.": "",
 "Yes. The shape and the name are what make it Theseus’ ship.": "",
 "It’s a river. Same and not the same.": "",
 "Doctor Agathe": "",
 "I did what we decided. I still don’t know if it was right.": "",
 "A dying man asks me about his son. His son died at sea last week; he doesn’t know. Do I tell him the truth, or let him die in peace?": "",
 "Tell him. He has a right to the truth.": "",
 "Let him go in peace. The truth can’t help him now.": "",
 "Ask him what he wants to know first.": "",
